WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:08.485
Soil Moisture Active Passive (SMAP) is a NASA environmental monitoring satellite that measures soil moisture across the planet.

00:08.971 --> 00:14.423
It is designed to collect a global 'snapshot' of soil moisture every 2 to 3 days.

00:14.951 --> 00:22.216
With this frequency, changes from specific storms can be measured while also assessing impacts across seasons of the year.

00:22.752 --> 00:27.447
SMAP was launched on 31 January 2015.

00:27.966 --> 00:36.239
It was one of the first Earth observation satellites developed by NASA in response to the National Research Council's Decadal Survey.
